{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-5c6d6ac8608f8c5233506476d0d94b904fe4582c22774f01","family_id":"KR:013050","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"ACT ON MANAGEMENT OF FIREFIGHTING EQUIPMENT","title_original":"소방장비관리법","kind":"법률","source_version":"245289","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=245289","source_sha256":"25ba510e1072cf12127e64686af78aaa90cbfc93d07098344d561859f48ffdd9","body_sha256":"95cb818e19adc080edea67c886327fc099427a237a26efd12529d73f5cf5ac8d","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 19 (Specification and Particular Specification of Fire Equipment) (1) The head of a fire service agency shall decide the name, item and specifications of fire equipment to be purchased.\n  (2) The head of a fire service agency may seek opinions from relevant experts or request necessary data from a manufacturer or importer, etc. of fire equipment in order to decide the name, item and specifications of fire equipment to be purchased.\n  (3) The head of a fire service agency may decide the particular specifications of fire equipment in consideration of special characteristics and quality of fire equipment to efficiently conduct fire service.\n  (4) Matters concerning the procedures and methods, etc. of deciding the specifications and particular specifications of fire equipment shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.","metadata":{"author_checks":["All current held source unit text, source editorial notes, amounts, periods, exceptions and source omission boundaries compared.","Unchanged official English retained only in the recorded exact source/target spans; original row, role, provider, edition, links and receipts remain unchanged.","New affected units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION / UNREVIEWED; source graphics remain linked to actual unchanged assets.","Source unit keys, order and full-text SHA matched the frozen inventory."],"author_method":"Exact v